# Source masters: the original, full-quality files that the shipped assets are
# derived FROM. They are not imported by any code and never reach a visitor.
#
# They are kept out of git on purpose. A 6MB video committed once stays in the
# history forever, on every clone, even after it is deleted — and the thing
# that actually matters, the derived files under src/assets/, is committed.
#
# The trade is that these live only on the machine that made them, so BACK
# THEM UP somewhere real (Drive, the photographer's original delivery). Losing
# a master means the encodes can never be regenerated at a different size or
# quality, only re-compressed from an already-lossy copy.
#
# Regenerate from a master with:
#   node scripts/make-image-variants.mjs <image master> --stem <name> --widths ...
#   (video encoding commands are documented in scripts/README.md)
masters/
